If you're using a *pure* Linux console (ie not in xterm or anything like
that), then the key is to switch the Linux charset for the slot nethack
uses (G0) to something useable. The way I do this is using the Linux
Console-Tools utilities; grab them from
http://lct.sourceforge.net/index.html. You should be able to get away with
installing them locally if you don't have root access to the box (though
don't take my word for that, worth a shot with --prefix=~/console-tools)

Anyways, once they're installed one way or another, switch the character
set to Codepage 437 (which is the default in MS-DOS) using the following
command:

charset G0 cp437

Then fire up Nethack and turn on IBMGraphics, which should now be working.
If you're using xterm of some sort, then the problem is somewhat
different, but I believe this solves your problem?

